## 4. Sales Strategy 2025: Operational Excellence

The 2025 strategy is built on three pillars: **Expansion**, **Efficiency**, and **Retention**.

### 4.1. Key Sales Metrics
Our customer acquisition cost (CAC) remains highly efficient at **AED 152,970** per new customer, contributing to our exceptional LTV:CAC ratio of 10.7.

| Customer Segment | Average Contract Value (ACV) |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hospitals | AED 735,000 |
| Clinics | AED 73,500 |
| Insurance Providers | AED 551,250 |

### 4.2. Retention and Churn Analysis
Maintaining and expanding our existing customer base is paramount. The following metrics must be used consistently in all sales and customer success communications.

| Retention Metric | Value (FY 2024) | Definition and Focus |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Logo Retention** | **87%** | Percentage of unique customer logos retained. Focus on preventing any customer loss. |
| **Customer Retention Rate** | **91%** | Percentage of total customer contracts retained. Focus on multi-product adoption. |
| **Gross Revenue Retention (GRR)** | **94%** | Revenue retained from existing customers, excluding expansion. Focus on minimizing downgrades. |
| **Net Revenue Retention (NRR)** | **118%** | Total revenue retained, including expansion (upsells/cross-sells). **Key growth indicator.** |

The NRR of 118% indicates that revenue expansion from existing customers significantly outweighs any churn or contraction. This is a critical talking point for all sales teams.

(For a deep dive into the underlying causes of churn and detailed action plans, refer to SALES-003: Churn Analysis).

